{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqiufl9zb2j","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Vendor '90% token savings' is strawman-relative; prompt caching already gives both arms memory-like cost","summary":"The audited ~90% memory-product savings compare against replaying full conversation history every turn — a baseline nobody competent runs. Under claude -p, prompt-cache reads bill at ~0.1x input and climb monotonically within a session, so the harness gives memory-like cost behavior to BOTH arms for free. Against real baselines the savings evaporate; cost difference was purely cache_read on the injected payload, with output tokens (real work) unmoved.","created_by":null,"valid_from":"2026-06-18T01:50:57.911Z","vec":[-0.003936794586479664,0.06964615732431412,-0.02914697304368019,-0.008149763569235802,0.007211169693619013,-0.017098430544137955,0.05586415156722069,0.07617200165987015,0.06827981770038605,0.09771179407835007,-0.009566000662744045,0.0495208278298378,0.047563303261995316,-0.07104703038930893,0.039464376866817474,-0.022749684751033783,0.11803444474935532,-0.04396373778581619,-0.018226973712444305,-0.004275825340300798,-0.01701514795422554,-0.03526795655488968,0.04807041212916374,0.07921094447374344,0.022618655115365982,-0.02531077340245247,-0.05461416020989418,-0.034314267337322235,0.06034715846180916,-0.02693714015185833,-0.02194083482027054,0.05225033313035965,-0.02692321315407753,-0.05568511784076691,-0.03652815520763397,0.061369117349386215,0.003190714167430997,-0.022540394216775894,-0.008456172421574593,-0.0270448736846447,-0.006902830675244331,-0.024052711203694344,-0.10925006866455078,0.07844945788383484,0.02956436015665531,0.04587046429514885,0.012283979915082455,0.01392572931945324,-0.09596848487854004,0.023814469575881958,0.0033793479669839144,-0.04115899279713631,0.022452011704444885,0.00040982800419442356,-0.08592589199542999,0.026317577809095383,-0.011095945723354816,0.04827244579792023,-0.04739043116569519,0.04706873372197151,-0.0567779466509819,-0.0